# Byte stability first. The harness digests committed resources (the hyphenation pattern it
# verifies by SHA-256, the golden manifest, the claims export) and compares generated pages
# byte for byte, so a checkout that rewrites their line endings breaks them: this is what made the
# Windows runner fail. Text files therefore keep LF everywhere, whatever the host's autocrlf says.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything the harness reads as bytes is never line-ending converted and never merged.
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.b64 binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.zip binary
*.ttc binary
*.woff2 binary
